nty"],["PRF calculator","/prf"]],"story":"<p class=\"prf-lede prf-story\">As of Oct 12, the record from 1951 to 2025 shows July to August came in under 90% of normal in 44 of 75 years on the middle value of the county&rsquo;s 10 grids. In 2025, September to October came in at 35% of normal and July to August at 42% on that middle. So far in 2026, the middle shows May to June at 240% of normal and April to May at 219%. Every grid had its driest year in 2011, with grid 9130 at 41%.</p>"}
